cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "p2p-peft-fl: Gossip / Epidemic P2P Federated PEFT for Text Classification"
abstract: >-
  A single-process simulator for peer-to-peer (serverless) federated learning
  that fine-tunes Transformer encoders (BERT / ALBERT / RoBERTa) on text
  classification datasets (AG News / SST-2 / IMDB) with LoRA adapters,
  exchanging only adapter weights over ring, random, fully-connected or grid
  topologies with gossip or epidemic message passing, mean / wlora / dlora
  adapter aggregation, and Dirichlet non-IID partitioning.
authors:
  - family-names: Dogani
    given-names: Javad
    affiliation: IMDEA Networks Institute
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/JavadDogani/P2P-decentralized-Federated-Fine-Tuning-of-LLM"
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - decentralized learning
  - peer-to-peer
  - gossip
  - parameter-efficient fine-tuning
  - LoRA
  - transformers
